{"action": "run_sql", "sql": "WITH RECURSIVE reach(inv_id) AS (SELECT id FROM inventories WHERE set_num='BIGBOX-1' AND version=1 UNION SELECT child.id FROM reach r JOIN (SELECT inventory_id, set_num AS child_num FROM inventory_sets UNION ALL SELECT inventory_id, fig_num FROM inventory_minifigs) e ON e.inventory_id=r.inv_id JOIN inventories child ON child.set_num=e.child_num AND child.version=(SELECT MAX(version) FROM inventories WHERE set_num=e.child_num)) SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT ip.part_num) AS n FROM reach r JOIN inventory_parts ip ON ip.inventory_id=r.inv_id WHERE ip.is_spare=false"}

This should work: reach collects all reachable inventory ids (root + nested sets' current inventories + minifigs' current inventories, recursively). Then count distinct part_num among non-spare parts. Let me run it.

